@node sb fiber lifecycle
@subsection Making and releasing fibers

A fiber made by @code{sb-fiber:make-fiber} is @code{:new} until first switched
to, @code{:runnable} while suspended, @code{:running} while it runs and
@code{:dead} once its entry function has returned. Registered fibers are
released when their thread exits; @code{sb-fiber:release-fiber} reclaims
one sooner.

@anchor{Function sb-fiber make-fiber}
@ffindex @sortas{make-fiber sb-fiber} make-fiber [sb-fiber]
@deffn{Function} sb-fiber:make-fiber function &key name stack-size binding-stack-size heap
Create a fiber that runs @code{function} (a zero-argument function or the
name of one) when first switched to.  @code{name} is a string label used by
@code{print-object}.

@code{heap}, if supplied, gives the fiber a local heap of its own: @code{t} creates
one with @code{make-heap}, or pass a heap from @code{make-heap} that no fiber owns
yet.  Everything the fiber allocates then belongs to that heap, which
is collected independently and released with the fiber.  @code{function} must
not itself be owned by a local heap.

When @code{function} returns, the fiber is marked DEAD and control switches
back to its most recent resumer, delivering @code{function}'s return value
as that resumer's @code{switch-fiber} value.

The calling thread must already have a current fiber.  Use
@code{make-main-fiber} or @code{with-fiber-thread} to establish one before calling
@code{make-fiber}.  Signals an error otherwise.

Fibers are auto-released when their owning thread exits; explicit
@code{release-fiber} is only needed if you want to reclaim resources sooner.
@end deffn
@anchor{Macro sb-fiber with-fiber}
@ffindex @sortas{with-fiber sb-fiber} with-fiber [sb-fiber]
@deffn{Macro} sb-fiber:with-fiber (var function &rest make-args) &body body
Create a fiber, bind it to @code{var}, execute @code{body}, release on exit.
@end deffn
@anchor{Function sb-fiber release-fiber}
@ffindex @sortas{release-fiber sb-fiber} release-fiber [sb-fiber]
@deffn{Function} sb-fiber:release-fiber fiber
Release @code{fiber}.  For a worker fiber, unmaps its stacks and frees the
bookkeeping struct.  For a main fiber, just frees the struct; the
thread's own stack and binding stack are untouched.  Signals
@code{fiber-state-error} if @code{fiber} is a worker that is still RUNNING.
Registered fibers are released automatically when their owning thread
exits.
@end deffn
