@node sb fiber interrupts
@subsection Interrupting a fiber

Fibers are not preempted. @code{sb-fiber:interrupt-fiber} stages a
condition that the fiber signals in its own context when it is next
resumed, or, for a fiber that has not run, before its entry function
starts.

@anchor{Function sb-fiber interrupt-fiber}
@ffindex @sortas{interrupt-fiber sb-fiber} interrupt-fiber [sb-fiber]
@deffn{Function} sb-fiber:interrupt-fiber fiber condition
Stage @code{condition} to be signalled in @code{fiber} on its next resume.
Cooperative -- nothing happens until @code{switch-fiber} delivers control
into @code{fiber}, at which point @code{condition} is signalled in the fiber's own
context.  A @code{new} fiber is effectively cancelled (the condition fires
before its entry function runs).
@end deffn
